From add59839e1cf8328c599029e7c55713fe78c3bb5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ingmar Stein <490610+IngmarStein@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 22:19:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(scrape): support scraping targets via Unix Domain
 Sockets

Add support for scraping targets via Unix Domain Sockets (UDS). When
the label __unix_socket__ is set on a target, the scrape client will
connect through the specified Unix domain socket instead of via the
target __address__.

The custom dial function is injected via config_util.WithDialContextFunc,
which ensures it is installed during transport construction before any
auth or TLS file-watching wrappers are applied. This avoids silently
falling back to TCP when file-based TLS, auth, or custom headers are
configured.

The dial function is prepended to the option list so that callers can
override it with their own WithDialContextFunc options.

Signed-off-by: Ingmar Stein <490610+IngmarStein@users.noreply.github.com>
